# Hide/Rearrange Consistency Always

For every UI touch in this repo (Standard/Minimal/Log-first/Field/HUD):

- Keep core controls reachable at launch and after any hide action.
- Every hide action must have an obvious restore path in the same window.
- Prefer reorderable controls where order affects daily workflow.
- Persist layout choices (order, visibility, docking position) per UI mode.
- Keep resize behavior deterministic: no jumpy reflow, no clipped primary controls.
- Avoid introducing UI states that can strand users without a recovery affordance.

Before finishing UI work:

- Verify hidden items are restorable without restarting.
- Verify reordered controls remain in the saved order on restart.
- Verify top-level actions remain visible at common laptop window sizes.
